From: Developer
Date: Thu, 06 Aug 2026
Subject: [PATCH] fix NewPipe red video layer by making Window.setStatusBarColor store state (https://gitlab.com/android_translation_layer/android_translation_layer/-/issues/66)

Bug: Window.getStatusBarColor() returned hardcoded 0xFFFF0000 (red), and
setStatusBarColor() discarded the value. NewPipe calls setStatusBarColor(Color.TRANSPARENT)
when entering fullscreen and then reads the color back — getting red and rendering a
red overlay on top of the video area.

Fix: Store the color in a private field, defaulting to 0xFF000000 (black), and
return the stored color from getStatusBarColor().

--- a/src/api-impl/android/view/Window.java
+++ b/src/api-impl/android/view/Window.java
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 
 	private Window.Callback callback;
 	private Context context;
+	private int statusBarColor = 0xFF000000;
 
 	public Window(Context context, Window.Callback callback) {
 		this.callback = callback;
@@ -119,7 +120,9 @@
 
 	public void takeSurface(SurfaceHolder.Callback2 callback) {}
 
-	public void setStatusBarColor(int color) {}
+	public void setStatusBarColor(int color) {
+		this.statusBarColor = color;
+	}
 
 	public void setNavigationBarColor(int color) {}
 
@@ -145,7 +148,7 @@
 		setBackgroundDrawable(context.getDrawable(resId));
 	}
 
-	public int getStatusBarColor() { return 0xFFFF0000; }
+	public int getStatusBarColor() { return this.statusBarColor; }
 
 	public Context getContext() {
 		return context;
